-- title:
--   Crossing presentation at an end: Hasse germ along V
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Further, $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota_0\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota_0\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, and `hK` fixes it as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base ring $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; `hAq` requires $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and `hξA` that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise image in $L((t))$ of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\prod$-normalised $j$-series. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ is fixed by `hϖ`, and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies `hϖt`: $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ (the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$), with distinguished element `jChartFin` $=j$. A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ is given with $\varpi\in y$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidity-and-presentation package, asserted for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras), every germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ pulled back along `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`-image $z$ at which the supersingularity condition of the previous paragraph holds for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. Under these hypotheses it provides a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u\big)$, subject to seven riders (summarised here), written in terms of the completion map $\mathrm{toC}$, the quotient map $\mathrm{mkS}$ and the germ map $\mathrm{germY}\colon C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ coming from the identification of $C$ with the global sections of `XFin` along the open immersion `ιFin`: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ that is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M')`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) $H$ — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_1,g_1$ of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, all $x\in K$ represented by the corresponding quotient of $q$-expansions, and every embedding $\iota$ of $L$ in $\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the identity $\iota(\tau x)\cdot(g_1|_k\gamma^{-1}\text{-conjugate }q\text{-expansion})=(f_1|_k\gamma^{-1}\text{-conjugate }q\text{-expansion})$ holds — preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ whose restriction to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$, $\theta$ fixing the constants, $\theta(X_{jj})\equiv\sum_{ii}M_{ii\,jj}X_{ii}$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M\equiv c\,\gamma$ entrywise modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ each omitting one of the images of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the image of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ differ; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ of this shape with tangent direction $(1,0)$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the Hasse germ clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and its class lies in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with that class congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is a unit at every $(a,b)$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, such that the image of the germ of that class minus $a_0$ equals $\mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   A specific $z,\varpi_z,y'$ as above is fixed, together with `hy'y`: $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$, and a specific presentation $(W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1)$ of the same shape; `hW₁` asserts for this presentation exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) just listed, with $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$ in place of $W,\sigma,e$, and $S$ now the quotient $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$.
--
--   The ideal $J$ of $C$ is fixed by `hJ` as the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau|_C^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0$ and $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, as $\gamma$ ranges over $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ that preserve $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is fixed by `hB` as the algebra generated over $C$ by all $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$, and $\mathcal W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypotheses on this pair are: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a fraction of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most one; `hR3` (five clauses), that $\mathcal W\cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $\mathcal W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$, and that $\mathcal W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}\cap B$, compatible with reduction on $A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms through an element $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c\neq1$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ non-trivial; that level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image under some such automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ of the $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$-locus; that an element of $B$ all of whose such conjugates lie in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $\mathcal W$.
--
--   Finally, the Hasse data are fixed explicitly: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ (`hjK`) and in $C$ (`hjC`), $a_0\in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y$ (`ha₀`), $e_0\ge1$, $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}\subseteq W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with the degree-$e_0$ form of $h$ a unit at every pair $(a,b)$ in $W_1$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ (`hhu`), and `hgerm`: $e_1$ applied to the completed germ of the class of `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` minus $a_0$ equals $\mathrm{mkS}\,h$. An integer $m\ge1$ is given with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$ (`hmt`). Lastly, $\mathcal O$ is a subring of $K$ subject to `hO`: there is $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the algebra generated over $C$ by all $x\in K$ with $xa\in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $\mathcal O$ the localisation $\{f\in K:\ fh\in B_a\text{ for some }h\in B_a\setminus P\}$, every element of $y$ a non-unit of $\mathcal O$, and $B\not\subseteq\mathcal O$; moreover $\mathcal O\subseteq\mathcal W$ (`hOW`), $\mathcal O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), $C\subseteq\mathcal O$ (`hCO`), and $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ (`hϖO`).
--
--   Under all of these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of elements $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$, a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota\colon \widehat{\mathcal O}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\big(\widehat A,\ \widehat\varpi^{\,m}\big)=\widehat A[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(X_0X_1-C(\widehat\varpi^{\,m})\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal O}$ and $\widehat A$ denote the adic completions of $\mathcal O$ and $A$ at their maximal ideals and $\widehat\varpi$ is the image of $\varpi$ in $\widehat A$, together with units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   1. $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $\mathcal O$ (with $\varpi$ taken as the element of $\mathcal O$ given by `hϖO`);
--
--   2. for every $a\in A$ whose image in $K$ lies in $\mathcal O$, $\iota$ sends that image in $\widehat{\mathcal O}$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\widehat A$;
--
--   3. $\iota$ of the image of $c_x$ equals $\gamma_U\cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U`;
--
--   4. $\iota$ of the image of $c_y$ equals $\gamma_V\cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`;
--
--   5. if $c_y$ lies in $\mathcal W$ then it lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$;
--
--   6. if $c_x$ lies in $\mathcal W$ then it does not lie in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$;
--
--   7. the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18)$-a_0$ lies in $\mathcal O$, and there are an integer $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of the image of that element equal to $w_V\cdot(\mathrm{UVCrossingModel.V})^{e}$.
--
--   The exponent $e$ in the last clause is not asserted to be $e_0$.
--
--   This is the statement, at an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q\ell)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, that the completed local ring of the end carries a crossing (node) presentation $\widehat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ over the base in which the branch coordinates are realised by elements of the ring itself and the Hasse germ $j-a_0$ becomes a unit times a positive power of the $V$-coordinate. It produces the presentation-specific form of that reading, and is cited by the companion statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_apply_jqNModC_sub_eq_unit_mul_V_pow_of_end_blowupChart_of_moduliHasse_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_apply_jqNModC_sub_eq_unit_mul_V_pow_of_end_blowupChart_of_moduliHasse_linked), which asserts the corresponding reading for an arbitrary crossing presentation.
